hash-shell (52-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * docs: drop the Product Hunt badge; the book catches up with the shell
  * fix(parser): expand aliases while parsing, and what modernish found next
  * fix(parser): $v"ro" keeps the variable's name boundary; $1 in $(( )) is text
  * fix(builtins): read assigns shell variables, not environment entries
  * fix(builtins): a listing that cannot be written fails; jobs says nothing without jobs
  * fix(expand): ${var#word} and ${var%word} expand their word; the battery's other finds
  * fix(expand): real 0x01..0x04 bytes survive expansion (marker collision)
  * fix(case): backslashes and quoted pattern characters in words and patterns
  * fix(exec): an empty matched case clause has status 0; eval of nothing succeeds
  * fix(builtins): command keeps break, continue, return and exit in effect
  * fix(varexpand): special parameters in braces and quotes, and a stable $$
  * fix(builtins): unalias -a, several names, and -- (POSIX)
  * fix(builtins): cd takes -L, -P and --, and keeps $PWD current
  * fix(lineedit): keep what was typed while a command ran (typeahead)
  * docs(site): say what hash is good at, with a conformance figure CI writes
  * feat(prompt): presets picked with set prompt=NAME, and the rest of bash's escapes
  * feat(execute): did-you-mean after "command not found" at the prompt
  * feat(builtins): help, with the text kept next to each builtin
  * feat(lineedit): vi editing mode with set -o vi
  * feat(completion): variables, directories, name spaces, git, make, man, and a complete builtin
  * fix(history): one entry per command, however many lines it took
  * fix(exec): refuse function nesting past FUNCNEST or the stack instead of crashing
  * test(modernish): second conformance suite, weekly, with a baseline
  * docs(install): the .deb download names use a dot, not a tilde

